message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "cerebral-hemodynamics-aspiration: lumped-parameter model of cerebral venous aspiration and intracranial pressure"
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
authors: [{family-names: "Assefa", given-names: "Adisu Mengesha", affiliation: "Department of Biomechanics, University of Nebraska at Omaha"}]
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adisu4/cerebral-hemodynamics-aspiration"
license: MIT
abstract: "Python implementation of a lumped-parameter model of intracranial hemodynamics, cerebrospinal fluid dynamics, and extracranial venous drainage, extending the models of Ursino and Lodi and Gadda et al., used to simulate flow-controlled aspiration at different locations along the cerebral venous outflow pathway in post-traumatic intracranial hypertension."
keywords: ["intracranial pressure", "cerebral venous outflow", "lumped-parameter model", "Starling resistor", "venous aspiration", "traumatic brain injury"]
